=== The Dragon Fight ===
After 8 [[Summoning Eye]]s have been placed, there will be a brief period before the dragon will hatch from an egg in the sky, knocking all players a large distance away from the Dragon Altar at the center of the [[Dragon's Nest]]. After the dragon has spawned, the dragon variant will be announced in the chat.

The door to the [[Dragon's Nest]] will shut, the gaps at the top will be covered with glass and 5 [[Ender Crystal]]s will spawn around the nest on top of obsidian spikes.

Additionally, [[Gregory]] the Opportunist will spawn near the [[Dragon's Nest|Dragon's Gate]]. He will sell a [[Decent Bow]] as well as Arrows at a higher price than the [[Weaponsmith]] in town.

==== Ender Crystals ====
At the start of a Dragon Fight, 6 Ender Crystals will spawn in 6 of 10 locations. Ender Crystals cause the dragon to heal {{Stat|hp|+0.3%}} per second if they are connected to the dragon. Every tick, there is a {{Green|10%}} chance for the crystals' connections to the dragon to be refreshed. If the dragon is within 32 blocks of any crystal, the crystal begins to heal it. Destroying a crystal rewards its destroyer with {{Item|Crystal Fragment|amount=1}} and {{Red|1,000}} Dragon {{Stat|dmg}} contributed. Destroyed crystals will respawn after 1-2 minutes, and can only respawn 3 times.

=== Attacks ===
The dragon has three attacks, which all deal {{Stat|True Damage}}. When under {{Stat|hp|50%}}, they deal {{Green|50%}} more damage.
# {{AN|Rush}} - The dragon will charge a player, inflicting {{Stat|dmg|2,000}}, {{Stat|tdmg|550}}, and {{Stat|knockback}}.
# {{AN|Fireball}} - The dragon will fly to a point in the arena, stop in place, then fire a barrage of fireballs at players. These fireballs explode and can damage multiple players at once. They will deal {{Stat|dmg|1,700}}, {{Stat|tdmg|200}}, and knock players high up into the air.
# {{AN|Lightning}} - The dragon will briefly stop in place, summoning lightning around it and creating audible thunder sounds. After a brief period, it will summon lightning and smite players from above, dealing {{Stat|dmg|1,700}} and {{Stat|tdmg|200}}. This attack can be avoided if the player has a block above their head.

If the player comes into contact with the dragon, they will receive {{Red|50%}} of their {{Stat|hp}} + {{Red|2,000}} in {{Stat|dmg}}.

After some time has passed, the dragon will summon groups of [[Zealot]]s. These [[Zealot]]s are immediately hostile, even if the player has not damaged or looked at them. The Dragon also makes already existing Zealots hostile.

When players are killed, they must make their way down to the [[Dragon's Nest]] again, and break down the sealed door. The door has lots of health, can be attacked with both ranged and melee attacks and will open again when its health bar is depleted. Both endermites and endermen spawn as the door takes damage. This can be avoided by using a {{Item|Rat Pet}}, {{Item|Armadillo Pet}}, or [[Travel Scrolls#Dragon Nest|Dragon's Nest Travel Scroll]].

After the Ender Dragon is defeated, [[Gregory]] will depart and hostile mobs will not spawn in the [[Dragon's Nest]] for a brief amount of time. All existing mobs within the Nest, including [[Voidgloom Seraph]] and [[Necromancy]] mobs, will instantly despawn. During this time, dragons cannot be summoned. After this brief time has passed, a message in the chat will announce the respawning of the Dragon Egg, after which mobs will spawn as normal and players are able to summon another dragon.

